# Red Kite - what the published installer and its two files should be.
#
# Checked by hand, before running the installer as root:
#
#     sha256sum rk-hub.sh
#
# and compared with the hub.sh line below. This copy lives on GitHub, which is NOT the machine
# that serves redkite.info - so somebody who gets into that machine cannot change both.
#
# The guide saves the installer as rk-hub.sh, and it is listed here under the name it is published
# under, hub.sh. So compare the two lines by eye - "sha256sum -c" against this file will say FAILED
# on a name it cannot find, which looks far more alarming than it is.
#
# The installer carries the other two checksums inside itself and refuses a file that does not
# match, which catches a stale CDN copy or a partial compromise. It cannot catch a replaced
# installer. That is what the line above is for.
92b137a17cf49a032312c7d1933d7a61554ee637a195c274f8aae1965d1b8897  hub.sh
8cd848d6348d5daee301af35cfb68c032b3274f59969c51fac03c738d7a9d1e6  docker-compose.yml
